    "caption": "😁 Figma Puts Product Specs Beside Designs\n\nFigma launched Specs, a Markdown editor for product requirements and technical documentation inside Figma, including design rules. Files can sit beside mockups on the same canvas. Design elements and FigJam diagrams can be embedded, with code blocks too.\n\nThe material becomes context for teams and AI agents. Teams can attach screen designs to an app description, then ask an agent to generate an interface or code. An agent can also inspect a finished design and produce technical documentation.\n\nThrough MCP, Specs pulls context from GitHub and analytics tools, then sends updates to systems such as Linear. The open beta is rolling out gradually to paid and education users.\n\n📊@tech",
